{"id": "EUVD-2026-81873", "enisaUuid": "17a54d41-5191-334d-aab2-bde75255f52b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nphy: qcom: qmp-usb: Fix possible NULL-deref on early runtime suspend\n\nThere is a small window where the runtime suspend callback may run\nafter pm_runtime_enable() and before pm_runtime_forbid(). In this\ncase, a crash occurs because runtime suspend/resume dereferences\nqmp->phy pointer, which is not yet initialized:\n        `if (!qmp->phy->init_count) {`\n\nThis can also happen if user re-enables runtime-pm via the sysfs\nattribute before qmp phy is initialized.\n\nSimilarly to other qcom phy drivers, introduce a qmp->phy_initialized\nvariable that can be used to avoid relying on the possibly uninitialized\nphy pointer.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:00:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b28287c5dea7650e6dd317591b9e82b6e145365", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f4e39ab1b2009a89c60e4cb9dbefb8140d405eff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5547fd950d6bf72de861b6934341e7bb0888640c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03455404fb6cbfd65842695df26739853fc1516b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/142c5593379273264474f31d5956b1a0065cd576"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gqgx-j6qf-xqf5", "CVE-2026-90280"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2566b0d4-6fef-31a0-aeab-c99e3b0f5aed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e464a3180a43b6596bd267f9f274e1793bfb8150 <142c5593379273264474f31d5956b1a0065cd576"}, {"id": "4dd15558-1d80-3906-adbe-f89b57f62cba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e464a3180a43b6596bd267f9f274e1793bfb8150 <03455404fb6cbfd65842695df26739853fc1516b"}, {"id": "4e5053e5-26ad-36cf-a525-01795499280b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "5daaad4d-34c4-377f-8b18-02ec638972cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "68bc33ff-48bc-3488-b6d9-2cb1ae32afb5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "9ebdab24-7f02-3920-9f66-67b0f189145d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "c32be1e6-a7d2-38e8-843c-14b0169488e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e464a3180a43b6596bd267f9f274e1793bfb8150 <9b28287c5dea7650e6dd317591b9e82b6e145365"}, {"id": "d8fe64ab-59ec-38c1-a7f5-2887e66dd49d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e2e23dd6-e567-3476-aba2-11b64d5efe19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "e431f1f3-3a33-37fd-b452-5815bd2275ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e464a3180a43b6596bd267f9f274e1793bfb8150 <5547fd950d6bf72de861b6934341e7bb0888640c"}, {"id": "f2f6a302-5b6f-3d8a-9840-8e89765e98a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e464a3180a43b6596bd267f9f274e1793bfb8150 <f4e39ab1b2009a89c60e4cb9dbefb8140d405eff"}, {"id": "fa1acaa4-55e5-34be-b83c-06aee7dad870", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d72db9a4-f62f-3d3b-b7de-217664656cfa", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}